{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The waterproof contact adhesive feels useful because my Gorilla tape and vinyl cement purchases suggest repairs where a flexible bond matters.",
    "Heat shrink tubing complements the crimp terminals I bought by protecting wiring connections, while the epoxy offers a stronger option for rigid repairs."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The safety can and glow sticks serve needs I have not shown; buying repair supplies does not mean I currently need liquid storage or emergency lighting.",
    "Butyl tape needs a particular sealing job, and nuts and washers need the right sizes. Their general usefulness is not enough for me to choose them now."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My Gorilla tape purchases seem to have been taken as a reason to suggest other Gorilla products, but a 24-pack of super glue exceeds any need I have identified.",
    "My hose clamps seem to have been interpreted as broad interest in plumbing and hardware supplies, even though clamps do not establish a need for thread seal tape or assorted fasteners."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The repair function matters: protecting electrical connections, bonding flexible materials, and strengthening rigid parts are different needs.",
    "Quantity and fit matter before I buy. My previous bulk purchases do not mean I need every supply in bulk, and fasteners must match the actual repair."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognize my practical repair interests, but sometimes assume a specific project or quantity without enough evidence."
}"}
